<title>ITALY: IBCA assigns AA+ rating for Italian regional bond.</title>
<headline>IBCA assigns AA+ rating for Italian regional bond.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>European rating agency IBCA has assigned a long term AA+ rating to a regional bond of 18.2 billion lire issued by the Piedmont region in north-west Italy last December.</p>
<p>According to the IBCA, it was not possible to assign the highest rating of AAA to an Italian region because there does not exist a formal mechanism to guarantee the payment of the bond's coupon from the regions, said a statement from the Piedmont region.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
